            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-evb/meta-evb-arm/meta-evb-fvp-base/recipes-phosphor/health/files/bmc_health_config.json",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Ideally this would be automated based on the file system type rather than it getting copied to multiple machines.  It looks like this one was copied from meta-ibm?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-evb/meta-evb-arm/meta-evb-fvp-base/recipes-phosphor/health/files/bmc_health_config.json",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "System uses `phosphor-mmc-init`, so it mounts the rwfs on `/var`, instead of `/run/initramfs/rw` (which is the default monitoring path in phosphor-health-monitor).\n\nSo should we make the changes in phosphor-health-monitor to change the monitoring path based on the fs type?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-evb/meta-evb-arm/meta-evb-fvp-base/recipes-phosphor/health/files/bmc_health_config.json",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "There are the \"distro features\" for MMC and various SPI-NOR flash layouts: `df-phosphor-mmc`, `df-obmc-static-norootfs`, `df-obmc-ubi-fs`.  This can be used to trigger a different default JSON file in the phosphor-health-monitor recipe.\n\nIf we want to do it as a recipe-level tweak or a meson-option, I think either could work.  I would lean towards a recipe-level though because the different file system / layouts is more of an OS/Distro level decision than a repository to me."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-evb/meta-evb-arm/meta-evb-fvp-base/recipes-phosphor/health/files/bmc_health_config.json",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the inform. Created the PR for recipe-level tweak - https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/85574"
                }
            ],
